      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "When I take pictures I only need to for people close to me to have their dynamic bones active. If they are far from me I don't need it bogging down my performance so I like this idea.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-12-10T21:34:51.430Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Add a slider to pick Dynamic Bone disable distance, allowing users to have Dynamic Bones disable closer to them optionally would improve performance greatly on slower per-core CPUs such as high-end Ryzen CPUs.\n\nFrom my own testings, Dynamic Bones can easily consume >2ms frame time.\n\nFor some perspective for those who don't know: For an Index @ 120Hz, you'd need 8ms or less frame time to achieve 120 FPS. Now think about that and about the 2ms from this single avatar. :)",
